course: dictionary
lesson: 8627
title: Scruff
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scruff is a noun, and it has two meanings. In the sentence «The Rat grips Toad by the scruff of the neck and hauls him up into his hall, dripping with mud and weed.» the clues are grips, hauls and dripping with mud. Grabbing someone and pulling them up tells you the scruff is the loose skin at the back of the neck.
explain: Look at the words around scruff. Gripping, hauling and mud all point to a rough, physical grab, not a hairstyle or a piece of clothing. Ask: what would fit here? Try «by the back of the neck» in the sentence instead, and see if it still makes sense. It does.
explain: The second meaning is about a person. A scruff is an untidy, dirty-looking person. This is informal British English, so you would use it with friends, not in a formal letter. «A little scruff» is a playful way to describe a messy child.
fact: Scruff means the loose skin at the back of an animal's neck.
fact: Mother cats carry their kittens by the scruff.
fact: «By the scruff of the neck» means grabbing someone roughly by the back of the collar.
fact: A scruff can also be an untidy, dirty-looking person. This is informal, UK English.
fact: «A little scruff» is a playful way to describe a messy child.
exercise: «The Rat grips Toad by the scruff of the neck.» What does scruff mean here? | A type of hat | A dirty old coat | A loud shout | *The loose skin at the back of the neck
exercise: Mother cats carry their kittens by the scruff. What is the scruff? | The soft bed | The tail | The front paws | *The loose skin at the back of the neck
exercise: In UK English, Mia says her little brother is a scruff after he plays in the mud. What does scruff mean? | A brave explorer | A pair of muddy boots | *An untidy, dirty-looking person | A kind teacher
test: Which phrase means grabbing someone roughly by the back of the collar? | At the top of the stairs | By the tail | *By the scruff of the neck | Under the bed
test: Which word is an informal UK word for an untidy, dirty-looking person? | *scruff | scrap | scream | scarf
exam: Read: «The Rat grips Toad by the scruff of the neck and hauls him up into his hall, dripping with mud and weed.» Which meaning of scruff fits? | *The loose skin at the back of the neck | A type of weed | A hall carpet | A dirty-looking person
